      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "18",
          "section": "4. Conclusions",
          "quote": "The novel six-component Al 10 Hf 25 Nb 5Sc 10 Ti 25 Zr 25 at.% high entropy alloy having complex microstructure was developed and cast by arc melting from the elemental precursors.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "12",
          "section": "3.5 Analysis of alloy composition using d-electron approach",
          "quote": "The Al 10 Hf 25 Nb 5Sc 10 Ti 25 Zr 25 alloy with Bo ≈ 2.87 and Md ≈ 2.49 values locates under the Ms=RT line, to the right from the Mf=RT line. ... Thus, it can be suggested that the Bo-Md diagram is an adequate tool for predicting the structure and deformation mode of the Al 10 Hf 25 Nb 5Sc 10 Ti 25 Zr 25 alloy.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 20",
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "12",
          "section": "3.4 Mechanical properties",
          "quote": "Room temperature tensile strength testing was carried out to determine the deformation mode of the Al 10 Hf 25 Nb 5Sc 10 Ti 25 Zr 25 alloy. The stress–strain plots for the as-cast state (continuous line) and after annealing at 1000°C for 5 h (dashed curve) are shown in Fig. 15a. An evident difference in the behavior of the as-cast and annealed Al 10 Hf 25 Nb 5Sc 10 Ti 25 Zr 25 alloy is observed. For the as-cast state, an average tensile strength reaching 900 MPa, (continuous curve) is accompanied by the strain of 4.2 %, while the yield strength and hardness amount to 500 MPa and 390 HV, respectively. Annealing leads to significant increase of the tensile strength, reaching up to 1240 MPa, while the yield strength and plasticity increase to 660 MPa and 11.5%, respectively. The hardness of the sample increases to 485 HV.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 15a",
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "12",
          "section": "3.4 Mechanical properties",
          "quote": "The as-cast Al 10 Hf 25 Nb 5Sc 10 Ti 25 Zr 25 sample during the uniaxial compression tests (Fig. 15b) showed a dual-yielding effect with the “primary” yield point of 620 MPa, fracture strength of 2132 MPa, and the overall plastic strain of 20%.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 15b",
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "12",
          "section": "3.4 Mechanical properties",
          "quote": "After the annealing of the sample, it revealed 1940 MPa at the yield strength of 1168 MPa.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "12",
          "section": "3.4 Mechanical properties",
          "quote": "The hardness of the as-cast and subsequently annealed alloy increase to 520 HV and 540 HV for the samples elongated by ε = 4.2% and 11.5%, respectively.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        },
        {
          "page": "14",
          "section": "4. Conclusions",
          "quote": "The alloy in the as-cast state consists of large grains with size up to 1000 mm within bcc cell dendritic structure and dimensions of 20-40 µm. Very fine orthorhombic needle-like structure with thickness up to 50 nm and length reaching 1 µm is revealed within cell grains.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "5f3374c1dbfde363:part:002"
        }
      ]
